{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"capacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Int","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every array reserves a specific amount of memory to hold its contents."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"When you add elements to an array and that array begins to exceed its","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"reserved capacity, the array allocates a larger region of memory and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"copies its elements into the new storage. The new storage is a multiple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the old storage’s size. This exponential growth strategy means that"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"appending an element happens in constant time, averaging the performance","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of many append operations. Append operations that trigger reallocation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have a performance cost, but they occur less and less often as the array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grows larger."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example creates an array of integers from an array literal,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then appends the elements of another collection. Before appending, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array allocates new storage that is large enough store the resulting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":